{"about": "Every answer of the only gate merges: the refusal of the merge authorisation leads to a copy of the merge step, which merges and delivers too. A gate guards a stop point, not one transition: one that cannot keep the run from every write of it guards nothing, so the four writes are refused.",
 "definition": "definitions/feature.json",
